### HIGH: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `server.js:93`
![security-high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/security-high-priority.svg) ![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `checkAuth` function is vulnerable to an unauthenticated denial-of-service (DoS) attack. `crypto.timingSafeEqual` throws a `TypeError` if the input buffers have different lengths. While line 92 checks that the string lengths of `provided` and `token` are equal, this does not guarantee that their byte lengths (when converted to UTF-8 buffers) are equal. For example, if `provided` contains multi-byte UTF-8 characters, its byte length will exceed its character length. An unauthenticated attacker can send a specially crafted `Authorization` header to trigger this exception, which, being unhandled in the async request handler, will crash the Node.js process.

```javascript
  const providedBuf = Buffer.from(provided);
  const tokenBuf = Buffer.from(token);
  if (providedBuf.length !== tokenBuf.length) return false;
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(providedBuf, tokenBuf);
```

