### MEDIUM: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `server.js:282`
![security-medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/security-medium-priority.svg) ![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `handleDispatch` function is vulnerable to an authenticated denial-of-service (DoS) attack. If the request body is the literal string `"null"`, `JSON.parse` returns `null`. Destructuring `null` on line 264 will throw a `TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'repo' of 'body' as it is null`. Since this exception is not caught in the main server handler, it will crash the process. An authenticated attacker can exploit this to disrupt the service.

```javascript
  if (!body) {
    res.writeHead(400, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: 'invalid body' }));
    return;
  }
  const { repo, prompt, model, branch } = body;
```

