crypto.timingSafeEqual but must compare UTF-8 byte lengths to avoid exceptions
for non-ASCII tokens; change the logic around authHeader/provided/token to build
buffers with the same encoding (e.g., Buffer.from(provided, 'utf8') and
Buffer.from(token, 'utf8')), compare their .length (or use Buffer.byteLength)
and only call crypto.timingSafeEqual when the buffer lengths match, returning
false otherwise (use the existing variables provided and token to locate the
check).
```

</details>

